# Moss turf 1: a wide, low patch of moss about 1.1 m across and 0.25 m tall, a flat cushion of dark humus under a hummocky
# mat of deep olive and teal moss, seven pale grey-green lichen crusts lying on its crown and five rounder hummocks of bright moss
# pushing up round them. A ground cover to scatter at the feet of trees and rocks, the moss counterpart of grass-turf1.
# Few, chunky shapes rather than a bristle of fine ones, so it stays light enough to scatter by the hundreds.
format 1

# Detail as the grass and flowers have it: the fine stalks and thin stems are small next to the model's size
